    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0367" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">632.6231/68: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-08T19:00:00-03:00">June 8, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 8—5:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>150. My 147, June 6, 8 p.m., numbered paragraph 2. Exchange of notes<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d237-f1"/> was effected today prolonging most-favored-nation
                    treatment between Brazil and Germany pending conclusion of a commercial
                    treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d237-f1" n="17" xml:id="d237-f1-content">
                <p>This agreement of June 8, 1936, between Brazil and Germany replaced the agreement
                    of October 22, 1931; for text of the 1936 notes, see telegram No. 152, June 10,
                    1 p.m., from the Ambassador in Brazil, <ref target="#pg269">p. 269</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
